<title>GERMANY: Linde details H1 unit sales, orders.</title>
<headline>Linde details H1 unit sales, orders.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996 (in millions of marks unless stated). Linde gave the following breakdown of sales development at its four main business divisions</p>
<p>Plant construction</p>
<p>    Sales					  373    down  7.8 pct</p>
<p>    Incoming orders			    711    up   10.6 pct</p>
<p>Cargo handling equipment</p>
<p>    Sales					1,896    up   12.5 pct</p>
<p>    Incoming orders			  1,889    down  2.8 pct</p>
<p>Refrigeration technology</p>
<p>    Sales					  420.1  up   12.9 pct</p>
<p>    Incoming orders			    522.1  up   19.3 pct</p>
<p>Technical gases</p>
<p>    Sales					 1,258   up	6 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German engineering group is Linde AG. The group said its plant construction sales were affected by usual swings in business volumes and that demand had remained lively. Full-year sales in the division should rise five percent to 1.3 billion marks, Linde said. The fall in incoming orders in cargo handling was due to sharply lower demand for hydraulics products and the weak German construction market.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
